10a:T46f2,## General note and mandatory information

**1. Name and contact details of the person responsible for processing and the company Data Protection Officer**

This data protection information applies to data processing by the controller:

plastship GmbH\
Auf der Lind 10\
65529 Waldems\
represented by Andreas Bastian and Markus Dambeck

Phone [+49 6126 58 980 10](tel:+4961265898010)\
Email [info@plastship.com](mailto:info@plastship.com)

**2. Terminology**

plastship uses the following terms in this data protection policy:

**a) personal data**

Personal data is any information that relates to an identified or identifiable natural person (hereafter: your, yours, etc.). A natural person is considered to be identifiable who, directly or indirectly, in particular by association with an identifier such as a name, an identification number, location data, an online identifier or one or more special features, expresses the physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity of this natural person can be identified.

**b) affected person**

Affected person is any identified or identifiable natural person whose personal data is processed by the responsible person.

**c) processing**

Processing is any process or series of operations related to personal information, such as collecting, organizing, storing, adapting or modifying, reading out, querying, using, with or without the aid of automated procedures, disclosure by submission, dissemination or other form of provision, reconciliation or association, restriction, deletion or destruction.

**d) responsible person or person responsible for processing**

The responsible person or person responsible for processing is the natural or legal person, public authority, institution or relevant authority, alone or collective with others, decides on the object and means of processing personal data. Where the purposes and means of such processing are determined by Union law or the law of the Member States, the responsible person or the specific criteria for his designation provided under union law or national law.

**e) processors**

A processor is a natural or legal person, public authority, institution or relevant authority that processes personal data on behalf of the responsible person.

**f) recipient**

Recipient is a natural or legal person, public authority, institution or relevant authority to whom personal data is disclosed, whether or not it is a third party. Authorities which may receive personal data under Union or national law in connection with a particular investigation assignment are not considered to be recipient.

**g) third party**

Third party is a natural or legal person, public authority, institution or relevant authority other than you, the responsible person, the processor and the persons authorized under the direct responsibility of the responsible person or the direct responsibility of the processor to process the personal data.

**h) agreement**

Agreement is each of you voluntary given consent , in a specific case, in an informed and unequivocal manner in the form of a statement or other unambiguous confirmatory act that indicates to you that you consent to the processing of your personal data.

**3. Collection and storage of personal data when you visit the website**

**a) When you visit our website**

When you access the website [plastship.com](/), the browser on your device automatically sends information to our server. This information is stored temporarily in log files. The following information is collected without any action on your part:

- IP address of the requesting computer
- date and time of access
- address requested and result of the request
- website from which the access is made (referrer URL), if your browser transmits it
- browser and operating system used

Purposes: establishing and maintaining a stable connection, detecting and defending against attacks and malfunctions, troubleshooting. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest follows from these purposes. We do not use the logs to draw conclusions about you as a person. The server logs are deleted automatically after 90 days.

We also use technically necessary cookies and — only with your consent — anonymous reach measurement. You can find more details in Sections 8 and 9 of this privacy policy.

**b) Contact form and enquiries**

If you write to us using the contact form, we process your details (name, email address, phone number, company, topic and optional details such as material, volume, application and postcode) and your message in order to answer your enquiry. Your enquiry is first stored in our own database on our servers at Hetzner Online GmbH in Germany and from there passed on as a case to our customer relationship management system Salesforce (Salesforce, Inc.; see Section 4), where our team handles it; if your email address is already assigned to a contact there, we link the enquiry to that contact. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where your enquiry relates to a contract or pre-contractual steps, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in answering enquiries). We store the enquiry for as long as necessary to handle it and any resulting business relationship, and then delete it unless statutory retention obligations apply.

**c) Protection against automated requests (ALTCHA)**

To protect our forms against spam and automated attacks, we use ALTCHA, a method that we operate ourselves on our own servers. Your browser solves a small computational task; no cookies are set and no data is transferred to third parties. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (protecting our systems against misuse).

**d) Contact by email and phone**

If you contact us by email or phone, we process your details in order to deal with your request. Our email communication runs on Microsoft 365 (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited; see Section 4). The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR. We retain business emails in accordance with commercial and tax law obligations (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR).

**4. Disclosure of data, recipients and transfers to third countries**

Your personal data will not be transferred to third parties for purposes other than those listed below. We only disclose your personal data to third parties if:

- you have given your express consent pursuant to Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR,
- disclosure is necessary pursuant to Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims and there is no reason to assume that you have an overriding legitimate interest in your data not being disclosed,
- there is a legal obligation to disclose pursuant to Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR, or
- this is legally permissible and necessary pursuant to Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR for the performance of contractual relationships with you.

To operate our services we use service providers who process data on our behalf and according to our instructions (processors, Art. 28 GDPR):

- **Hetzner Online GmbH** (Germany): operation of the website, platform and database in data centres in Germany; encrypted backups in Finland (EU)
- **Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited** (Ireland; parent company Microsoft Corporation, USA): sending emails and email communication (Microsoft 365) and AI services (Azure OpenAI, Azure Speech)
- **Salesforce, Inc.** (USA, with group companies in the EU): customer relationship management (CRM), enquiries and business transactions
- **Functional Software, Inc. (Sentry)** (USA; data stored in the EU data region): detection of technical errors and, only with consent, performance measurement

For providers based in the USA or their group companies, access from the USA cannot be ruled out. For such transfers we rely on the European Commission's adequacy decision for the EU-US Data Privacy Framework (Art. 45 GDPR) where the provider is certified under it, and otherwise on the European Commission's standard contractual clauses (Art. 46(2)(c) GDPR). You can obtain a copy of the safeguards on request at [info@plastship.com](mailto:info@plastship.com).

**5. Extent of processing of personal data**

We process personal data of users only as this is necessary to provide a functional website as well as the content and services of plastship. The legal basis for each processing operation is stated with that operation; we only ask for consent where the law requires it.

**6. Legal basis for the processing of personal data**

As long as we have obtained your consent to the processing of personal data, the Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. a DSGVO serves as a legal basis.

In the processing of personal data, which is necessary for the fulfillment or completion of a contract or precontractual measures, the Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. b DSGVO serves as a legal basis.

To the extent that processing of personal data is required to fulfill a legal obligation subject to plastship, the Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. c DSGVO serves as a legal basis.

If the processing is necessary to safeguard a legitimate interest of plastship or of a third party and the interests, fundamental rights and fundamental freedoms of you do not outweigh the former interest, the Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. f DSGVO serves as a legal basis for the processing.

**7. Data deletion and storage duration**

The personal data of you will be deleted or blocked as soon as the purpose of the storage is omitted. In addition, it may be stored if provided for by the European or national legislator in EU regulations, laws or other regulations to which the controller is subject. A blocking or deletion of the data takes place even if a storage period prescribed by the mentioned standards expires, unless there is a need for further storage of the data for a contract conclusion or a contract fulfillment.

**8. Cookies and access to your device**

Cookies are small text files that your browser stores on your device. Under Section 25(1) TDDDG (German Telecommunications Digital Services Data Protection Act), storing information on your device and accessing it is only permitted with your consent, unless it is strictly necessary for us to provide the service you have expressly requested (Section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).

Without consent we only use such strictly necessary cookies:

- `next-auth.session-token` (on https with the prefix `__Secure-`, split into several parts `.0`, `.1` … for large sessions): login cookie that keeps your session; first-party cookie, up to 30 days, deleted when you log out; only after login
- `next-auth.csrf-token` (on https `__Host-next-auth.csrf-token`): protects the login against cross-site request forgery; first-party cookie, session duration
- `next-auth.callback-url` (on https `__Secure-next-auth.callback-url`): return address after login; first-party cookie, session duration
- `pr-csrf-binding`: protects the "reset password" process; first-party cookie, 1 hour
- `NEXT_LOCALE`: selected language; first-party cookie, 1 year
- `plastship_consent`: your decision in the cookie notice (`necessary` or `all`); first-party cookie, 1 year
- only on our non-public test and staging systems: `ps_zugang`, remembers the passed access check; first-party cookie, 180 days

The ALTCHA spam protection (Section 3 c) does not set any cookies. If you choose them yourself, we additionally store display settings (such as light or dark mode, sidebar, list views) and the selected language in your browser's local storage; they do not leave your device.

On your first visit, a notice asks whether you additionally agree to anonymous reach measurement (Section 9) and to measuring the technical performance of the website. We store your decision in the cookie `plastship_consent` for one year. You can change your decision at any time with effect for the future and withdraw consent as easily as you gave it: via the "Cookie settings" link at the bottom of every page, which reopens the notice ("Necessary Only" withdraws consent). The legal basis for necessary cookies is Section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG in conjunction with Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR; for purposes requiring consent it is Section 25(1) TDDDG in conjunction with Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR.

We do not use advertising cookies or third-party cookies. You can configure your browser to prevent cookies from being stored; however, you cannot log in to the platform without the necessary cookies.

**9. Reach measurement**

We do not use any third-party analytics, tracking or advertising services on our website. Only if you have agreed in the cookie notice do we count visits to public pages anonymously in our own database: we store the page visited, the page you came from and the time — without IP address, without user ID, without device fingerprint and without a dedicated identifier cookie. In this case we additionally record measurements of the technical performance of the pages (loading times) via Sentry (Section 4). The purpose is to understand which content is used and where the website needs technical improvement. The legal basis is your consent (Section 25(1) TDDDG, Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you can withdraw at any time (Section 8). The individual counts are deleted after 90 days; only daily totals remain thereafter.

For usage analysis within the logged-in application, see the "Additional information on the plastship application" below.

**10. Links to social networks and other websites**

Our pages contain simple links to other websites, for example to LinkedIn or YouTube. We do not embed any plug-ins, buttons or videos from these providers; no data is transmitted to them when you merely visit our pages. Only when you click such a link does your browser open the provider's page; from then on, the provider's privacy notice applies, for example [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy) or [YouTube/Google](https://policies.google.com/privacy).

**11. Rights of persons affected**

Your rights:

In accordance with Art. 15 GDPR, you have the right to demand information about the personal data on you that we process. In particular, you can demand information on the purposes of processing; the category of personal data; the categories of recipients to whom your data is or was disclosed; the planned storage period; the existence of a right to correction, erasure, limitation of processing or objection; the existence of a right of complaint; the source of your data if not collected by us; and the existence of automated decision-making including profiling and meaningful information about the details of this.

In accordance with Art. 16 GDPR, you have the right to demand the immediate correction or completion of your personal data stored by us.

In accordance with Art. 17 GDPR, you have the right to demand the erasure of your personal data stored by us, unless processing is necessary for exercising the right of freedom of expression and information, for compliance with a legal obligation, for reasons of public interest, or for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.

In accordance with Art. 18 GDPR, you have the right to obtain restriction of processing of your personal data where you contest the accuracy of the data, the processing is unlawful but you oppose its erasure, or we no longer need the data but you require it for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims, or you have objected to the processing in accordance with Art. 21 GDPR.

In accordance with Art. 20 GDPR, you have the right to obtain your personal data you provided to us in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format and to demand transmission of that data to another controller.

In accordance with Art. 7 Para. 3 GDPR, you have the right to withdraw your consent from us at any time. This will mean that we are not permitted to continue the data processing based on this consent in future.

In accordance with Art. 77 GDPR, you have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. You can usually do this by contacting the supervisory authority of your habitual residence or place of work, or the authority responsible for plastship: Der Hessische Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit (Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information), Wilhelmstraße 7, 65185 Wiesbaden, Germany, [datenschutz.hessen.de](https://datenschutz.hessen.de).

We do not make decisions based solely on automated processing, including profiling, that produce legal effects concerning you or similarly significantly affect you (Art. 22 GDPR).

**12. Right of objection**

Where your personal data is processed based on vital interests in accordance with Art. 6 Para. 1 Clause 1 lit. f GDPR, you have the right in accordance with Art. 21 GDPR to object to the processing of your personal data on grounds relating to your particular situation or where the objection is to direct marketing. In the latter case, you have a general right to objection, which we shall implement without specification of a particular situation.

If you would like to exercise your right of objection or withdrawal,it is sufficient to send an email to [info@plastship.com](mailto:info@plastship.com).

**13. Data security**

The connection to our website and to the platform is encrypted with TLS throughout (recognisable by "https://" and the padlock icon in your browser); unencrypted connections are redirected to encrypted ones.

We also use appropriate technical and organisational security measures to protect your data against accidental or deliberate manipulation, partial or complete loss, destruction or unauthorised access by third parties. Our security measures are continuously improved in line with technological developments.

**14. Up-to-dateness and amendment of this privacy policy**

This privacy policy is dated October 2026. Further development of our website and services or changes in statutory or regulatory requirements may make it necessary to amend this privacy policy. You can access and print the current privacy policy at any time on the website under [Privacy Policy](/privacy).

