181:T2e5b,## Additional information on the plastship application

**Collection and storage of personal data when accessing the application**

When you access the application, your browser automatically sends information to our server. This information is stored temporarily in log files and kept until it is deleted automatically:

- IP address of the requesting computer
- date and time of access
- address requested and result of the request
- browser and operating system used

Purpose: establishing and maintaining a stable connection, detecting attacks and malfunctions, troubleshooting. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest follows from these purposes. The logs are not used to draw conclusions about your behaviour and are deleted automatically after 90 days.

**Cookies**

The application only sets cookies that are strictly necessary for its operation (Section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG): a login cookie that keeps your session, technical cookies that protect against attacks, and cookies for your chosen language and your decision in the cookie notice (details in Section 8 above). The login cookie is valid for up to 30 days and is deleted when you log out. In addition to the session ID, it contains your user ID, email address, role, language and display setting so that the application can work without further queries.

No cookies are set for advertising or analytics purposes, and no data is transferred to advertising networks. The legal basis for processing cookie data is Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR.

**Logs within the application**

When you are logged in, the following events are stored in our own database; they do not leave our servers:

- **Logins and security events** (successful and failed logins, password changes, two-factor operations, logins from a new device) with IP address and browser. Purpose: protecting your account, detecting misuse. Legal basis Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Deleted automatically after 180 days.
- **Active sessions** with IP address, browser and time of last activity, so that you and administrators can end sessions. Expired sessions are deleted automatically every day, at the latest 30 days after login.
- **Record views** for users with the customer and agent roles: which records (such as orders, accounts, tasks) you have viewed, created or edited. Purpose: the "recently viewed" function in search and support by your contact persons; administrators can view this list per user. Deleted automatically after 12 months.
- **Business changes** (status changes, actions of the AI assistant) as evidence of who changed what and when. Kept for as long as the record exists.
- **Usage analysis**: which page of the application you open, when, and from which page of the application, as well as individual interactions without content (for example a click on a contact link, only type and location), with your user ID and role, without IP address, without browser data, without content or record IDs. Purpose: identifying which areas are used and which are not, in order to develop the application further. Evaluations are only made in aggregate per role; roles with fewer than five active persons are not shown separately. The data is not used to assess individual persons. Raw data is deleted after 90 days; after that only daily totals without personal reference remain. Legal basis Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. You can object at any time (Art. 21 GDPR): in your profile under "No usage analysis" or by email; your raw data is then deleted immediately. The measurement works without cookies and without storing anything on your device; usage by plastship test accounts is recorded but filtered out of all evaluations.

There is no recording of the screen, mouse movements or input.

**Error diagnostics (Sentry)**

To detect and fix technical errors, we use Sentry (Functional Software, Inc.) in the EU data region. If an error occurs in your browser or on the server, the following is transmitted: technical error details, the address accessed, browser and operating system and, to assign the incident, your user ID, email address and role. Your IP address is not transmitted; your session is not recorded. We only record measurements of loading times and performance (traces) if you have agreed in the cookie notice (Section 9 above). The data is deleted after 90 days. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (stability and security of the application); a data processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR has been concluded with Sentry. The provider is based in the USA; for transfers to third countries, see Section 4 above.

**Map views, address search and routes**

We operate maps, address search and route calculation (for example location maps, place fields, travel expenses and the map page for addresses) ourselves on our servers in Germany. The map data comes from OpenStreetMap (© [OpenStreetMap contributors](https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright), ODbL). Map tiles and fonts are publicly accessible and come exclusively from plastship; as with every page request, we process your IP address in the server logs (see above) and limit the number of requests per IP address to protect against misuse. We only process addresses and coordinates you enter in order to calculate results and routes; they are not stored and not transferred to third parties. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (performance of the contract or use of the platform) and otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in a functioning and protected platform). A map link next to an address opens our own map page. Only if you expressly click "Open in maps app" there will Apple Maps open on Apple devices, or the maps app you have set up on Android devices; the address and coordinates are then sent to that provider, and its privacy notice applies. Next to routes (for example in travel expenses and on the RIGK map) there is a link “Route in Google Maps”: only when you click it does Google Maps open in a new tab, and the start and destination (coordinates) are transmitted to Google (Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland); without a click there is no connection to Google, and our pages load nothing from Google. Google’s privacy policy applies to the processing by Google: [policies.google.com/privacy](https://policies.google.com/privacy).

**AI assistant (PIA) and other AI functions**

The AI assistant PIA is only available to plastship employees; it is labelled as AI in the interface, and its answers are generated by a language model. When employees use the assistant, their input and the records required for it — which may include details of customers, contact persons and transactions — are transmitted to a language model on Microsoft Azure OpenAI (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited) and are not used for training there; the user ID is only transmitted as a checksum (hash). For voice input and output, we use Azure Speech in the Germany West Central region. The conversation history is deleted after 90 days, the log of actions performed by the assistant after 180 days. The assistant does not make decisions about people; it only carries out actions at the request and under the control of employees.

We use the same Azure services to translate content of the website and the platform as well as interface texts into further languages, and to analyse photos of materials. Machine-translated versions of content are labelled as AI translations where they are displayed and link to the German original; AI analyses of material photos are labelled as well. Legal texts (terms and conditions, imprint, privacy policy, email disclaimer, accessibility statement) are never machine-translated; the German version is binding in each case. For translations, only the texts to be translated are transmitted; for analyses, only the photo. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR (efficient handling of transactions); a data processing agreement has been concluded with Microsoft; for transfers to third countries, see Section 4 above.

**Account and registration**

To use the platform, we create an account for you or you apply for one. In doing so, we process your personal and company details (name, business email address and phone number, company, address, position, language) and login data. We only store passwords as a hash; depending on the role, a second factor is mandatory. An account you have applied for only becomes active after you have confirmed your email address and plastship has approved it. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR. We store account data for the duration of use; you can request deletion of your account at any time at [info@plastship.com](mailto:info@plastship.com), unless statutory retention obligations prevent this.

**Verification of business partners**

Before we approve companies as business partners, plastship employees check their details against public sources (Art. 14 GDPR). For this purpose, our servers transmit the company name, VAT identification number, internet domain or website address and, where applicable, the name of a contact person to: the EU VAT Information Exchange System (VIES), commercial and company registers (OpenRegister, Companies House, GLEIF, OpenCorporates, Wikidata), sanctions lists (OpenSanctions), services for checking domains and websites (RDAP, Google Safe Browsing, VirusTotal, DNS blocklists) and — as a checksum of the email address — Gravatar; we also check with the domain's mail server whether a given email address exists. The purpose is protection against fraud, shell companies and sanctions violations; the legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR and, where sanctions law applies, Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR. The results are only a suggestion: plastship employees decide on approval, not an automated procedure. Customers only see whether a company has been verified.

**Customer relationship management (Salesforce)**

We keep company, contact person and transaction data (such as enquiries, requirements, offers, samples, orders, invoices and certificates) in our customer relationship management system Salesforce (Salesforce, Inc.); the platform reads and writes this data there. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR and, for the retention of business records, Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR (up to ten years under commercial and tax law). A data processing agreement has been concluded with Salesforce; for transfers to third countries, see Section 4 above.

**Emails from the platform**

We send system messages (such as login details, confirmations and notifications) via Microsoft 365. The platform does not send promotional newsletters. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.

**Auction house**

In the auction house, providers (manufacturers) auction batches to the distributors they have admitted; plastship operates the auction house, and the contractual partner for the purchase is the provider. For this we process account data, bids with amount and time, awards and logs. The provider sees bids with the name of the bidding company, not of the person acting; bidding companies do not see each other, and nobody sees maximum bids. Batch, status and price data, but no details of bidders, flow via the interface to the provider's system. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, for security and protection against misuse Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, and for retention Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR. We delete interface logs after 90 days.

**Data security**

The connection to the application is encrypted with TLS. The application is operated on servers of Hetzner Online GmbH in Germany; encrypted backups are also kept with Hetzner in Finland and are overwritten after 21 days. A data processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR has been concluded with Hetzner. We use Cloudflare exclusively for name resolution (DNS) of our domains; your data traffic does not pass through Cloudflare.

